## t97: Adaptive protection, in plain language, with editable rules
admin-protect-not-country = This protection looks only at how a client, mailbox or administrator uses the server: request volume and requests the server rejects. It does not use countries or devices; for those, see Sign-in country policy and Temporary sign-in locks.
admin-protect-summary-title = What happens today
admin-protect-summary-budget = Request budget: { $mode }.
admin-protect-summary-budget-off = Requests are not counted.
admin-protect-summary-budget-on = An address that is not signed in may make { $client } requests in every { $window }; a signed-in mailbox may make { $account } and a signed-in administrator { $admin }, wherever they connect from. Sign-in requests always count against the address. The next request over a budget is slowed down until the window ends. 0 means no budget for that kind.
admin-protect-summary-unusual = Unusual requests: { $mode }.
admin-protect-summary-unusual-off = Unusual requests are not counted.
admin-protect-summary-unusual-on = Counted as unusual: { $signals }. Action starts at { $shortCount } unusual requests or { $shortRatio } % of requests within { $shortWindow }, or at { $longCount } or { $longRatio } % within { $longWindow } (0 turns that trigger off).
admin-protect-summary-step = First the client is slowed down, then blocked.
admin-protect-summary-step-detail = The first time a trigger is reached, requests wait { $throttle }. If it is reached again before { $decay } pass without unusual requests, requests are refused for { $block }. Nothing is permanent.
admin-protect-summary-observe = In "Observe only", every action above is recorded in the history below but no request is slowed or refused. Use it to try a policy safely.
admin-protect-presets-title = Presets
admin-protect-presets-help = Start from a preset, check what it changes, then apply it. Exemptions and the storage failure behaviour are never changed by a preset.
admin-protect-preset-relaxed = Relaxed
admin-protect-preset-relaxed-help = Records what would happen without slowing anyone down, with generous limits.
admin-protect-preset-balanced = Balanced
admin-protect-preset-balanced-help = Enforces the built-in limits. Suits most servers.
admin-protect-preset-strict = Strict
admin-protect-preset-strict-help = Lower limits and longer blocks. For a server under attack or with few users.
admin-protect-preset-same = The current rules already match this preset.
admin-protect-preset-diff = What { $preset } changes
admin-protect-preset-apply =
    { $count ->
        [one] Apply 1 change
       *[other] Apply { $count } changes
    }
admin-protect-preset-applied = { $preset } applied.
admin-protect-diff-rule = Rule
admin-protect-diff-now = Now
admin-protect-diff-preset = Preset
admin-protect-readonly = You can see these rules but not change them. Changing them needs permission to write settings.
admin-protect-global-only = These rules apply to the whole server; they cannot be set per domain.
admin-protect-saved =
    { $count ->
        [one] Rule saved.
       *[other] { $count } rules saved.
    }
admin-protect-save = Save
admin-protect-saving = Saving…
admin-protect-save-rule = Save { $rule }
admin-protect-cancel = Cancel
admin-protect-reset = Reset to default
admin-protect-reset-rule = Reset { $rule } to its default
