admin-protect-signal-normal = An ordinary request
admin-protect-signal-malformed = Malformed request
admin-protect-signal-oversized = Request too large
admin-protect-signal-credential-rejected = Wrong password or key
admin-protect-signal-permission-denied = Permission denied
admin-protect-signal-body-deadline = Request body too slow
admin-protect-signal-admin-route-miss = Unknown admin console address
admin-protect-group-budget = Request budget
admin-protect-group-budget-help = A fixed number of requests per time window, counted across all server replicas.
admin-protect-group-unusual = Unusual requests
admin-protect-group-unusual-help = Requests the server rejects for a clear reason are counted over a short and a long window. Too many of them, or too high a share, starts an action.
admin-protect-group-actions = What happens
admin-protect-group-actions-help = How long a slow-down and a block last, and when a client starts again with a clean record.
admin-protect-group-exceptions = Exceptions and failures
admin-protect-group-exceptions-help = Who is never counted, and what to do if the counters cannot be read.
admin-protect-rule-rate-mode = Request budget
admin-protect-rule-rate-mode-help = Off: nothing is counted. Observe only: going over the budget is recorded. Enforce: going over it slows the requests down with "429 Too many requests".
admin-protect-rule-rate-mode-example = With Enforce and a budget of 600 per minute, the 601st request in a minute waits until the next minute.
admin-protect-rule-client-requests = Requests per address (not signed in)
admin-protect-rule-client-requests-help = How many requests one IP address may make in each window while not signed in, sign-in attempts included. Requests with a valid session use the mailbox or administrator budget instead. 0 turns this budget off.
admin-protect-rule-client-requests-example = 600 per minute is far more than a sign-in page needs, while a script sending thousands of anonymous requests is slowed down. Signed-in staff behind one office address are not affected.
admin-protect-rule-account-requests = Requests per mailbox
admin-protect-rule-account-requests-help = How many requests one signed-in mailbox may make in each window, across all its sessions, devices and addresses. Keep it above the per-address budget. 0 turns this budget off.
admin-protect-rule-account-requests-example = 1800 per minute leaves room for webmail, a phone and a desktop app syncing at once.
admin-protect-rule-admin-requests = Requests per administrator
admin-protect-rule-admin-requests-help = How many requests one signed-in administrator may make in each window. Keep it above the per-address budget. 0 turns this budget off.
admin-protect-rule-admin-requests-example = 1200 per minute leaves room for busy console pages while limiting a stolen admin session.
admin-protect-rule-rate-window-secs = Budget window
admin-protect-rule-rate-window-secs-help = The length of each budget window, in seconds. The count starts again at the start of each window.
admin-protect-rule-rate-window-secs-example = 60 means "per minute".
admin-protect-rule-adaptive-mode = Unusual request protection
admin-protect-rule-adaptive-mode-help = Off: nothing is counted. Observe only: actions are recorded but not applied. Enforce: clients that send too many unusual requests are slowed down, then blocked for a while.
admin-protect-rule-adaptive-mode-example = Use Observe only for a week, read the history, then switch to Enforce.
admin-protect-rule-signals = What counts as unusual
admin-protect-rule-signals-help = Only these rejected requests count. Ordinary "not found" answers, busy-server refusals and browser names never count.
admin-protect-rule-signals-example = Counting wrong passwords catches password guessing; counting unknown admin console addresses catches scanners looking for the console.
admin-protect-rule-adaptive-clients = Count per client
admin-protect-rule-adaptive-clients-help = Count unusual requests per IP address.
admin-protect-rule-adaptive-clients-example = A scanner trying many addresses from one IP is slowed down.
admin-protect-rule-adaptive-accounts = Count per mailbox
admin-protect-rule-adaptive-accounts-help = Count unusual requests per signed-in mailbox, from any address.
admin-protect-rule-adaptive-accounts-example = A mailbox whose session sends malformed requests from many addresses is slowed down.
admin-protect-rule-adaptive-admins = Count per administrator
admin-protect-rule-adaptive-admins-help = Count unusual requests per signed-in administrator.
admin-protect-rule-adaptive-admins-example = An admin session that keeps hitting refused pages is slowed down.
admin-protect-rule-short-window-secs = Short window
admin-protect-rule-short-window-secs-help = The recent period in which bursts are counted, in seconds.
admin-protect-rule-short-window-secs-example = 300 looks at the last 5 minutes.
admin-protect-rule-short-absolute-anomalies = Unusual requests in the short window
admin-protect-rule-short-absolute-anomalies-help = Act when this many unusual requests arrive within the short window, however many normal requests come with them. 0 turns this trigger off.
admin-protect-rule-short-absolute-anomalies-example = 20 wrong passwords in 5 minutes from one address starts a slow-down.
admin-protect-rule-short-ratio-percent = Share of unusual requests, short window
admin-protect-rule-short-ratio-percent-help = Act when unusual requests reach this percentage of all requests in the short window, once there are enough requests to judge. 0 turns this trigger off.
admin-protect-rule-short-ratio-percent-example = At 50 %, a client whose requests are half rejected is slowed down.
admin-protect-rule-short-minimum-samples = Requests needed to judge the share, short window
admin-protect-rule-short-minimum-samples-help = The share rule waits until at least this many requests were seen in the short window.
admin-protect-rule-short-minimum-samples-example = With 30, one rejected request out of two is not enough to act.
admin-protect-rule-long-window-secs = Long window
admin-protect-rule-long-window-secs-help = The longer period in which slow, patient attempts are counted, in seconds.
admin-protect-rule-long-window-secs-example = 604800 looks at the last 7 days.
admin-protect-rule-long-absolute-anomalies = Unusual requests in the long window
admin-protect-rule-long-absolute-anomalies-help = Act when this many unusual requests add up within the long window. 0 turns this trigger off.
admin-protect-rule-long-absolute-anomalies-example = 100 wrong passwords over a week catches someone trying a few passwords every hour.
admin-protect-rule-long-ratio-percent = Share of unusual requests, long window
admin-protect-rule-long-ratio-percent-help = Act when unusual requests reach this percentage of all requests in the long window, once there are enough to judge. 0 turns this trigger off.
admin-protect-rule-long-ratio-percent-example = At 25 %, a client with one rejected request in four over the week is slowed down.
admin-protect-rule-long-minimum-samples = Requests needed to judge the share, long window
admin-protect-rule-long-minimum-samples-help = The share rule waits until at least this many requests were seen in the long window.
admin-protect-rule-long-minimum-samples-example = With 100, a client that made only a few requests is never judged on its share.
admin-protect-rule-normal-cap-per-bucket = Limit on normal requests counted
admin-protect-rule-normal-cap-per-bucket-help = Caps how many normal requests are counted in each slice of a window, so a flood of valid requests cannot hide unusual ones.
admin-protect-rule-normal-cap-per-bucket-example = With 1000, sending thousands of valid requests does not dilute the share of rejected ones.
admin-protect-rule-throttle-secs = Slow-down
admin-protect-rule-throttle-secs-help = How long requests wait the first time a trigger is reached, in seconds.
admin-protect-rule-throttle-secs-example = 3 makes each request wait 3 seconds: barely noticed by a person, costly for a script.
admin-protect-rule-block-secs = Block
admin-protect-rule-block-secs-help = How long requests are refused when a trigger is reached again before the record is clean, in seconds.
admin-protect-rule-block-secs-example = 300 refuses requests for 5 minutes, then lets them through again.
admin-protect-rule-decay-secs = Clean record after
admin-protect-rule-decay-secs-help = After this many seconds without unusual requests, the next trigger is treated as a first time again (a slow-down, not a block).
admin-protect-rule-decay-secs-example = 86400 forgives after one quiet day.
admin-protect-rule-exempt-clients = Exempt addresses
admin-protect-rule-exempt-clients-help = IP addresses or networks that are never counted per client. Mailbox and administrator limits still apply. One per line.
admin-protect-rule-exempt-clients-example = 203.0.113.0/24 for an office whose staff all share one address.
admin-protect-rule-exempt-accounts = Exempt mailboxes
admin-protect-rule-exempt-accounts-help = Mailbox account IDs that are never counted per mailbox. Their client address is still counted. One per line.
admin-protect-rule-exempt-accounts-example = The ID of a monitoring mailbox that signs in every minute.
admin-protect-rule-exempt-admins = Exempt administrators
admin-protect-rule-exempt-admins-help = Administrator IDs that are never counted per administrator. Sign-in locks and session limits still apply. One per line.
admin-protect-rule-exempt-admins-example = The ID of an automation account that calls the admin API often.
admin-protect-rule-storage-failure = If the counters cannot be read
admin-protect-rule-storage-failure-help = What to do when an enforced limit cannot be checked because the database is unavailable.
admin-protect-rule-storage-failure-example = "Refuse the request" is safer; "Let the request through" keeps mail working during a database problem.
admin-protect-sim-title = What would happen?
admin-protect-sim-help = Describe a sample request and see what the rules would decide and which rule decides it. Nothing is stored and no counter changes.
